@startuml "Iterator - Org Chart (Solution) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title A department that gives out iterators

interface "Iterable<Employee>" as Iterable
interface "Iterator<Employee>" as Iterator {
  + hasNext() : boolean
  + next() : Employee
}
class Department <<Aggregate>> {
  - members : List<Employee>
  - units : List<Department>
  + add(Employee)
  + add(Department)
  + iterator() : Iterator<Employee>
  + byLevel() : Iterable<Employee>
}
class DepthFirstIterator <<ConcreteIterator>> {
  - departments : Deque<Department>
}
class LevelOrderIterator <<ConcreteIterator>> {
  - waiting : Deque<Department>
}
class ChangeReport {
  + firstDifference(before, after) : Optional<String>
}

Iterable <|.. Department
Iterator <|.. DepthFirstIterator
Iterator <|.. LevelOrderIterator
Department ..> DepthFirstIterator : creates
Department ..> LevelOrderIterator : creates
ChangeReport ..> Iterator : two at once

note right of Department
  <b>No getter for its lists.</b>
  Callers get an iterator and decide
  when to move and when to stop.
end note
note bottom of DepthFirstIterator
  A stack: department by department.
end note
note bottom of LevelOrderIterator
  A queue: level by level.
end note
@enduml
